      "repair": "The quay's polygonSlab side walls faced inward: the rubble (0-0.62 m) and plaster (0.62-1.2 m) rims of the mapped base, the plaster service-head walls (1.17-3.91 m) and the concrete deck edge (3.91-4 m). From outside the near walls were culled and the quay rim read as see-through (scan: stone part 98%, plaster 35%, model 16.5%). Root cause: polygonSlab in lighthouse-blacksea-models.mjs, and its copies in vorontsov-browser-model.mjs (district/street detail and the skyline service head), reversed each wall quad when the outline's signed (x, z) area was negative; an unreversed quad already faces the edge's left, which is outward for these clockwise outlines, so every wall was turned inward. Fix: reverse only for a positive signed area. Outlines, vertices and material assignment are unchanged; the generic wall UV projection follows the normal, so those walls' texture runs mirrored. Note: the previous binding (source sha256:4b5dbd6c..., 54,128 triangles) predates the 2026-10-26 tubePath cowl change (53,872 triangles); the recaptured frames include it and show continuous blue cowls.",
